---
name: progress-events
description: Test progress events with explicit roles and outcomes.
engine: 0.2.0-lab.1
roles: [lead, worker]
---
"""
The lead starts one piece of work. The worker may report progress, and must finish within ten
minutes of starting.
"""
contract @4h mentions 1 => expired

"""
You are the lead. Start the work, read the progress reports, and wait for the finish.
"""
role lead

"""
You are the worker. Report progress as a percentage while you work, and send finish within ten
minutes. Progress does not give you more time.
"""
role worker

"""
Start the work.
"""
type start

"""
Report how far along the work is, as a whole percentage.
"""
type progress
  percent: integer(0..100)

"""
The work is finished. Set start to the start this finishes.
"""
type finish
  start: ref(start)

"""
The lead has not started the work yet. Send start.
"""
state new
  """
  Start the work. The worker then owes one finish.
  """
  lead -> worker: start() awaits working
    """
    The worker finishes within ten minutes of the start.
    """
    => finish() & complete
     """
     No finish arrived within ten minutes of the start.
     """
     | @10m & stalled

"""
The worker is working and owes finish within ten minutes; progress reports are optional.
"""
state working

"""
Progress can be reported in any active state; it never extends a state deadline.
"""
anystate
  event worker -> lead: progress()

"""
The worker finished. Send nothing more.
"""
end complete

"""
The worker did not finish within ten minutes. Stop, and report where the work stands.
"""
end stalled

"""
The four-hour contract clock ran out. Send nothing more.
"""
end expired
